    "image_name": "swebench/swesmith.x86_64.benoitc_1776_gunicorn.bacbf8aa",
    "repo": "swesmith/benoitc__gunicorn.bacbf8aa",
    "problem_statement": "Worker signal handling broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe arbiter's `kill_workers` method is sending incorrect signals to worker processes. When attempting to kill all workers with a specific signal, the first worker gets killed twice (once with the intended signal and once with SIGTERM), while all other workers only receive SIGTERM regardless of the intended signal.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport signal\nfrom gunicorn.arbiter import Arbiter\nfrom gunicorn.app.base import BaseApplication\n\nclass DummyApp(BaseApplication):\n    def load_config(self):\n        pass\n    def load(self):\n        def app(environ, start_response):\n            start_response('200 OK', [])\n            return [b'']\n        return app\n\n# Create arbiter with some mock workers\narbiter = Arbiter(DummyApp())\narbiter.WORKERS = {1001: None, 1002: None, 1003: None}\n\n# Try to send SIGUSR1 to all workers\narbiter.kill_workers(signal.SIGUSR1)\n```\n\nExpected behavior: All workers should receive SIGUSR1\nActual behavior: First worker gets SIGUSR1 then SIGTERM, other workers only get SIGTERM\n\nThis affects graceful worker restarts and other signal-based worker management operations."
  }
}
